---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import WorkList from "@daviddef/archive-kit/components/WorkList.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import work from "../data/worklist.json";
const rows = work.rows;
const open = rows.filter(r => !["done", "struck"].includes(r.state)).length;
---
<Base title={work.title}
      eyebrow={`${rows.length} items, ${open} of them open`}
      dek={work.dek}>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p set:html={work.lead
      .replace(/\[([^\]]+)\]\((\/[^)]*)\)/g, (_m, t, h) => `<a href="${u(h)}">${t}</a>`)
      .replace(/\*\*([^*]+)\*\*/g, "<strong>$1</strong>")} />
    <p>The other registers on this site are about the family. <b>This one is about the work</b>, which
      means it is the only page here that is mostly about this archive's own limits &mdash; what it is
      waiting on, what it cannot reach, and what it set out to do and had to strike because the plan
      rested on something untrue.</p>
    <p class="cap">{work.close}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>The list</h2>
  <WorkList work={work} u={u} />
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>What does not go here</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Findings do not. This archive already has five registers for those and they are better at it:
      <a href={u("/searched/")}>what has been read</a> holds every query ever run, negatives at the same
      length as finds; <a href={u("/open-questions/")}>open questions</a> holds what is not known, with
      the record set that would answer each; <a href={u("/errands/")}>errands</a> holds what can only be
      got by standing in a reading room; <a href={u("/corrections/")}>corrections</a> holds every claim
      withdrawn and the cause; and <a href={u("/changes/")}>what changed</a> holds the diary.</p>
    <p><b>None of them answered what is being done</b>, and so for weeks that answer lived in a chat
      window &mdash; which is the one place that does not survive the session. That is the whole reason
      for this page, and it is the same failure this archive keeps finding in its sources: the material
      survives and the index to it does not.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
